{"amendments":[{"body":"`crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:232-239` now emits `nitrogen_cycle.total_n_nitrified_mg`, but the value it logs is still `nob_step + comammox_step` from `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:343-346`, while alkalinity is consumed on the AOB leg as well (`crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:236-240,371-384`). In a partial-nitrification tick (for example AOB active, NOB absent or O2-limited), the trace will show positive `alk_consumed_meq` with `total_n_nitrified_mg=0`, which makes the new diagnostics scientifically wrong and breaks the intended stoichiometric attribution.","rationale":"This is a correctness issue in the newly exposed trace output: the reported nitrified load can disagree with the alkalinity debit exactly when nitrite accumulates."},{"body":"The new bookkeeping surface is still one-sided, so it does not actually prepare the denitrification return path. `NitrogenCycleOutput` only exposes `alkalinity_consumed_meq` (`crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs:12-23,382-384`), and the trace schema only writes `nitrogen_cycle.alk_consumed_meq` (`crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs:236-238`). Once denitrification is added, there is no place to report 'consumed X / returned Y' separately without adding another public struct field and trace key or overloading the existing field with a different meaning.","rationale":"Because `NitrogenCycleOutput` is public, adding the missing return-path field later is a real API/schema change; keeping only a net or consumed-only value would lose the per-path attribution this bead was supposed to make ready."}],"summary":"Reviewed the inner worktree changes and relevant tests. Found one correctness bug in the new nitrification trace diagnostics and one significant API/bookkeeping gap around the promised denitrification return path."}